# /etc/age-offsite-backups/recipients.txt on the BACKUP HOST.
#
# Public keys only: one age recipient per line, comments start with #.
# Get each line by running, on the machine where that private key lives:
#   age-keygen -y restore-key-1.txt
# and paste the age1... output below. Never copy a line that starts
# AGE-SECRET-KEY- onto the backup host; backup-push refuses to run if one
# is here.
#
# Restore key 1: held by the person on call, on the recovery machine
# age1...
#
# Restore key 2: offline copy, kept somewhere else
# age1...
